  "description": "H(v) for a spread of JSON values, as 64-character lowercase hex. An implementation that reproduces every entry has the Merkle hash right, which is what makes its table keys agree with Python's. Note `int_large` (9007199254740993) and the int/float pair 0 vs 1.0: a language that parses all JSON numbers as doubles cannot reproduce these and therefore cannot host a conforming *encoder*, only a decoder.",
